  - name: "Superior Strength and Endurance"
    description: "Exceptional physical strength and stamina, reflected in the 5D6 P.S. and 5D6 P.E."
  - name: "Claws, Kick and Head Butt"
    description: "Claws or punch 2D6 damage plus P.S. damage bonus. Kick 3D6 S.D.C. damage plus P.S. damage bonus. Head butt 3D6 damage."
  - name: "Horn Charge"
    description: "A charge with the horns does 5D6 S.D.C. damage plus P.S. damage bonus and has a 60% chance of knocking the victim down; a victim knocked down loses one melee attack and initiative."
  - name: "Languages"
    description: "Every Minotaur speaks Troll/Giantese, Gobblely and Elven. Most (94%) are illiterate."
restrictions:
  - "Magic comes only through an O.C.C. and is very limited."
  - "94% of all Minotaurs are fighters of one sort or another (printed 50)."
extraction_notes: |
  - Printed 48-50. The entry opens under the Lazretheg on printed 48 and its stat block, headed "Intelligent Humanoid", ends on printed 50 above the Mologoth. Neither monster is part of this class.
  - Attributes as printed (50): I.Q. 2D6+1, M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 5D6, P.P. 4D6, P.E. 5D6, P.B. 3D6, Spd 3D6.
  - S.D.C. reads "2D4x10 plus those gained from physical skills", so the 2D4x10 is a POOL BONUS rather than sdc_base.
  - Natural A.R. 12 is stored as prose in natural_abilities; Horror Factor 14 is the top-level horror_factor.
  - Attacks per melee prints "2 or by O.C.C.", stored as attacks_base: 2: a starting number, and the higher of it and a Hand to Hand style''s stands.
  - Bonuses printed: +1 to strike, parry and dodge, +3 to save vs Horror Factor, in addition to attribute and skill bonuses. All four stored. This book prints no strike bonus for the horns.
  - Damage as printed: the kick and the horn charge say "plus P.S. bonus", the claws/punch say "plus P.S. bonus", and the head butt prints 3D6 with no P.S. bonus named. Stored as prose exactly so.
  - Recognize scent 22% and track by blood scent 54% are printed with no plus sign and no per-level gain, and the catalog has no skill row for either; stored as prose in Superior Sense of Smell.
  - Languages prints "All Minotaurs speak Troll/Giantese, Gobblely and Elven. Most (94%) are illiterate", with NO percentage. Stored as prose in a Languages natural ability rather than as skills, because no figure is printed to store. The catalog rows a later decision would use are "Language: Troll/Giant", "Language: Gobblely" and "Language: Dragonese" (Dragonese/Elven).
  - O.C.C.s Available states proportions, not limits: 94% take a man at arms O.C.C. (40% of those mercenaries, 20% assassins, knights and palladins extremely rare) and 6% a clergy or man of magic O.C.C. Nothing is barred, so no occ_restrictions is written. The page names Chaos Priest, Disciple of the Old Ones, Necromancer and Earth Warlock and refers to the Old Ones sourcebook for them.
  - Magic prints "Only by O.C.C., very limited; 94% of all Minotaurs are fighters of one kind or another" (printed 50); both halves are restrictions lines.
  - Psionics prints "Standard, same as humans", so no psionics block and no psionics_allowed line.
  - Printed 215: Minotaur use the experience table of their chosen O.C.C., so no xp_table is stated.
  - Size prints 8 to 11 feet, "7 feet +1D4 additional feet". In the Lore.
  - The entry prints no money or equipment line; none is stated.
  - Alignment prints "Any, but most are evil or selfish", which is not a restriction, so no evil tag.
